<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83257" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πῑσα</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πίση</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πίσα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ης</span>, ἡ, a fountain at Olympia (<i><span class="en">
			Str.
			8.3.31
		</span></i>), which gave a name to Olympia itself, <i><span class="en">
			Stesich.
			90
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>O.</u>
			1.18
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			2.7
		</span></i>, etc.: Adv.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πίσηθεν</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			7.390
		</span></i> (Antip. Thess.); <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πισαῖοι</span></b> , οἱ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the people of Pisa</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				15.82
			</span></i> : Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πισαῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				74.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.350
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Crin.
			</span></i>), etc.:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πισάτης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				9.68
			</span></i> ; fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πισᾶτις</span></b> ,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
			ἐλαία</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				4.13
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Πισᾶτις</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				8.3.3
			</span></i> ; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Πισαία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paus.
					5.1.6
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<u>Pisa</u> in Etruria, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.16.2
			</span></i>, etc.: elsewh. in pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πίσαι, αἱ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.27.1
			</span></i>, etc. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πῐσα</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i>, in other Poets <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πῑσα</span>.]</div>
